Looking at this problem, I need to determine whether there exists a constant $C(p) > 0$ depending only on $p$, with $C(1) = 1$, such that $\mathbb{E}[(X - \mathbb{E}[X])^{2p}] \leq C(p)\,\mathbb{E}[X^{2p}]$ for all even integer orders $p = 1, 2, \ldots$.

